  ('a5571e94-f74c-5db1-ad7f-e406ebed1b7a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-precise-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Read the sentences: "Lucia wore her rain boots. The hiking trail was muddy." Which choice best combines the sentences to show how the ideas connect?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Lucia wore her rain boots because the hiking trail was muddy.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The hiking trail was muddy because Lucia wore her rain boots.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"Lucia wore her rain boots, but the hiking trail was muddy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-connector"},{"text":"Lucia wore her rain boots, the hiking trail was muddy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice-unfixed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Lucia wore her rain boots because the hiking trail was muddy.$q$, $q$The mud is the reason for the boots, so "because" shows the link. The choice "The hiking trail was muddy because Lucia wore her rain boots." flips cause and effect, as if the boots made the trail muddy.$q$, 'draft', null)
