   $q$Read the sentences: "Monarch butterflies migrate each fall. They fly to Mexico. They travel thousands of miles." Which choice best combines all three sentences into one clear sentence?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Each fall, monarch butterflies migrate thousands of miles to Mexico.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Monarch butterflies migrate each fall they fly to Mexico and they travel thousands of miles.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"run-on"},{"text":"Each fall, monarch butterflies travel thousands of miles to Mexico to find food.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-new-facts"},{"text":"Each fall, monarch butterflies fly to Mexico.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each fall, monarch butterflies migrate thousands of miles to Mexico.$q$, $q$This sentence keeps the season, the distance and the place, with no repeated "they." The choice that ends "to find food" is smooth, but "to find food" is a new reason the original never gave.$q$, 'draft', null)
