   $q$Ayaan wrote this to his principal: "Hey, can we get a recycling bin for the art room? Thx!" Which revision best fits a letter to a principal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Can we get a bin? Thx for reading this!","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-informal-abbreviation"},{"text":"Could the school please add a recycling bin and a new sink to the art room? Thank you.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-new-facts"},{"text":"Could the school please add a recycling bin to the art room? Thank you for considering it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Yo, we really need a recycling bin in the art room right now!","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-informal"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Could the school please add a recycling bin to the art room? Thank you for considering it.$q$, $q$"Could the school please" and "Thank you" are polite, formal wording that keeps the same request. The choice that adds "a new sink" is formal too, but it asks for a sink that Ayaan never mentioned.$q$, 'draft', null)
