   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (3) as the claim of the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Relay races are held at many track meets in the spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-claim"},{"text":"A baton is usually made of metal or hard plastic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-claim"},{"text":"Kowalczyk thinks that every school should start a track team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Kowalczyk shows that a good baton pass can matter as much as how fast each runner is.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kowalczyk shows that a good baton pass can matter as much as how fast each runner is.$q$, $q$The whole draft explains how the handoff saves time, and sentence 12 says teamwork matters as much as speed, so this claim fits. The draft never says Kowalczyk wants every school to start a team.$q$, 'draft', '2a272bdc-2330-5f95-bb1a-7648febe0f1d')
