insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b5789e6c-67c6-5d5f-9a9a-bace3dff6e7a', 'wg6-argument-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-argument-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Walk to School Fridays$q$, $q$(1) Each morning, a long line of cars crawls past Brookside Middle School, and the air near the entrance smells of exhaust. (2) Brookside should start Walk to School Fridays, when students who live nearby walk or ride bikes in groups led by adult volunteers. (3) Walking gives students exercise before class begins. (4) Students who are active in the morning often find it easier to pay attention in class. (5) Fewer cars would also mean cleaner air and safer streets near the school.

(6) Some parents worry that walking to school is not safe. (7) ______ each walking group would follow a set route with crossing guards at the busiest corners. (8) One adult volunteer would walk at the front of each group and another at the back.

(9) Others argue that students would arrive late. (10) Groups would leave from meeting spots at set times, so arrivals could be more predictable than the car line.

(11) Walking to school would make Brookside healthier and calmer. (12) Plus, my friend Dante said it sounds fun.$q$, 'draft')
