        '6-8', $q$Building a Cup Telephone$q$, $q$(1) A cup telephone is a simple project that shows how sound travels. (2) First, gather two paper cups, a sharp pencil, and a piece of string about ten meters long. (3) ____, poke a small hole in the bottom of each cup with the pencil. (4) Push one end of the string through each hole and tie a thick knot inside the cup so the string cannot slip out. (5) Paper cups are also useful for planting seeds on a sunny windowsill. (6) Finally, walk away from your partner until the string is pulled tight.

(7) When you speak into one cup, your voice makes the bottom of the cup shake back and forth very quickly. (8) These tiny shakes, called vibrations, travel along the tight string. (9) When they reach the other cup, its bottom shakes in the same pattern. (10) As a result, your partner hears your words. (11) If the string sags, however, the vibrations fade and the message is lost.$q$, 'draft')
