        '6-8', $q$Playing Fair Without a Referee$q$, $q$(1) Ultimate is a team sport played with a flying disc, and it has one unusual rule. (2) In most games, there is no referee on the field. (3) ____, the players call their own fouls and settle their own disagreements. (4) If a player believes someone pushed them, that player calls out "Foul!" and play stops. (5) The two players then talk about what happened and decide together how to continue.

(6) Some people worry that this system would lead to cheating. (7) In practice, players learn that honesty keeps the game fun for everyone. (8) Many teams even give an award to the opponent who showed the most fairness. (9) The disc is usually made of light, smooth plastic. (10) Teams also gather in a short circle after each game, where both sides share what went well. (11) ____, ultimate teaches players that being trusted matters as much as winning.$q$, 'draft')
