  ('7464e737-a5d8-57de-be73-25e761869a0a', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Why is sentence 5 important to paragraph 1?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It explains what the evidence in sentences 3 and 4 means, so readers see how it supports the claim.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It adds a new fact from the article that the writer has not mentioned anywhere else.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-analysis-evidence"},{"text":"It shares a personal experience that makes the paragraph more interesting to read.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sentence-purpose"},{"text":"It names the title and author of the article that the whole draft is about.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sentence-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It explains what the evidence in sentences 3 and 4 means, so readers see how it supports the claim.$q$, $q$Sentence 5 tells readers that returning to the same forests without a guide means monarchs have a built-in compass, which is analysis of sentences 3 and 4. It is tempting to call it a new fact, but the facts come from sentences 3 and 4 and sentence 5 explains them.$q$, 'draft', '57c6f2bc-8caf-5da4-a17a-ba763a6c770e')
