   $q$The writer wants to add one more piece of evidence to support sentence 7. Which detail from the article would work best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Okafor describes the large wooden screens that workers used to dry each wet sheet.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-point"},{"text":"Okafor mentions that some paper was dyed red or blue with juice from plants.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-evidence"},{"text":"Okafor says that modern factories can make millions of sheets in one hour.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-point"},{"text":"Okafor explains that students in some schools practiced writing on slates so they would not waste paper.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Okafor explains that students in some schools practiced writing on slates so they would not waste paper.$q$, $q$Sentence 7 says people treated paper with care, and practicing on slates to save paper is another example of that care. The drying screens are part of how paper was made, which supports paragraph 1, not sentence 7.$q$, 'draft', '29ffc352-e7dd-5e28-84ac-45689addf0a8')
