values
  ('abd3ae75-2602-5812-9228-bd28bf8330a4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-writing-with-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence 10 that explains how it supports paragraph 2. Which sentence works best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This shows that coaches enjoy watching their young players at the end of a season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-evidence"},{"text":"This shows that the quick choices players practiced on small fields turned into better decisions during games.","is_correct":true},{"text":"This shows that players touch the ball more often when they play on smaller fields.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-point"},{"text":"This shows that every young player who uses a small field will become a star.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This shows that the quick choices players practiced on small fields turned into better decisions during games.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 is about thinking quickly, and smarter passes are evidence that quick decision practice paid off. The idea about more touches is true in the draft, but it explains paragraph 1, not sentence 10.$q$, 'draft', '9ddeec85-6a0e-54b0-b4a3-cb4c9f2dc948')
