   $q$Which sentence best fills blank (11) as the conclusion of the draft?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Delgado reports that the waste dropped from forty pounds to about fifteen pounds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-without-analysis"},{"text":"Delgado's article shows that when students share in planning lunch, they waste less and learn to make careful choices.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Pizza should be served every day because it is the lunch that most students like best.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Many schools around the world serve very different kinds of lunches to students.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Delgado's article shows that when students share in planning lunch, they waste less and learn to make careful choices.$q$, $q$The conclusion should bring together both points, less waste and new skills, and only the choice saying students waste less and learn to make careful choices does that. Restating the drop in pounds repeats evidence from paragraph 1 instead of closing the whole analysis.$q$, 'draft', '1f43b476-1777-55fc-a3eb-dd2219c2ef77')
